      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T19:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m curious, why does Servo_V4 have 50ms when this has 161 (going to 121ms)? I didn\u0027t expect there to be that much of a change\n\nAdded Sam as well due to his work on TCMPv2 which may be impacted.",
      "revId": "2f43a762c0e59958d94ef4e37d6745ddd8c8db4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ac27311_5afc0f93",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T19:42:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please see the image attachment here:\nb/211845598#comment13\n\nNote the gap between \"when VBUS hits 20v\" and \"when PS_RDY is relayed (line)\".\nThe line\u0027s location is hardcoded; the voltage curve depends on charger.\n\nWe were hitting problems with the 50ms value on Apple 96w charger.\nThe PS_RDY was being relayed *before* the Apple charger had ramped.\n50ms resulted in us \"slamming\" the Apple charger during a voltage transition.\n(Spec violation of \"7.3.3 Increasing the Voltage and Current\" pSnkStdby)\n\nScope current traces showing this are available elsewhere.",
      "parentUuid": "c221e35d_94e5c45d",
      "revId": "2f43a762c0e59958d94ef4e37d6745ddd8c8db4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
